cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "CRNL — Chemical Reaction Network Landscape"
message: "If you use this software or its measured results, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Panteleimon-Panagiotis
    family-names: Christou
    alias: Pantelis
repository-code: "https://github.com/Pantelis23/CRNL"
abstract: >-
  A simulation rig for making signal restoration measurable. The same chemical
  reaction network is run deterministically (mass-action ODEs) and stochastically
  (exact Gillespie SSA), and the gap between them is the subject. Results include
  the restoration wall P(error) ~ exp(-c(eps)*Omega) with c(eps) = (3/2)eps^2
  derived from the saddle geometry; a chemical freeze-out transition under volume
  expansion; the free-energy cost of restoration from exact chemical master
  equation solves, including the bifurcation at gamma_c = 1/2 where a landscape
  costs a minimum affinity of 3 ln 2; and a crossover between the restoration
  wall and an Omega-independent channel floor that sets a maximum cascade depth.
keywords:
  - chemical reaction networks
  - approximate majority
  - Gillespie algorithm
  - stochastic thermodynamics
  - signal restoration
  - chemical master equation
license: Apache-2.0
